From 7f9ad5c1f344be45daec915ed1191f4ddbb63967 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:58:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reverb: Digital plate model, low and high cut, Mutable and
 Freeverb fixes

- Digital: Dattorro's plate (Griesinger topology), after the community
  firmware's model (#3277) but following the paper: real allpasses in the
  tank, one damping filter per half, delays scaled up to 44.1 kHz (x1.45 to
  share the 32768-sample buffer), Width as stereo width, decay and level
  matched to Mutable at the default settings.
- Mutable: LFOs at Mutable Instruments' rates (they ran 16 times slower:
  stepped once per read, and without the x32 in the constructor), the AP1
  smear back in, damping running from bright (0) to dark (50) like
  Freeverb's (1.2.1 ran it backwards, with a jump between 0 and 1).
- Low cut (HPF) with the right coefficient (it reached 85 Hz instead of
  520), now applied when a song loads; new high cut (LPF), off at 50.
- Freeverb: balanced left and right below full Width, and saturating
  instead of wrapping when a long reverb gets too loud.
- Song files: damping stays in 1.2.1's direction on disk, the old "hpf" and
  the community firmware's "lpf" are read at the cutoffs they actually had,
  the new values go in "lowCut" and "highCut"; songs from community 1.3,
  which turned the damping round too, are read in its direction. The
  reverb presets on the reverb button keep their 1.2.1 sound.
- Host fallback of signed_saturate matches ssat (host builds only).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
